Lab Tasks
Task 1: Content-Based Router Pattern
Objective: Route messages to different endpoints based on message content

Create a new Java class ContentBasedRouterDemo.java:
import org.apache.camel.builder.RouteBuilder;
import org.apache.camel.main.Main;

public class ContentBasedRouterDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Main main = new Main();
        main.configure().addRoutesBuilder(new RouteBuilder() {
            @Override
            public void configure() throws Exception {
                from("direct:start")
                    .choice()
                        .when(header("priority").isEqualTo("high"))
                            .to("stream:out?promptMessage=High priority message: ")
                        .when(header("priority").isEqualTo("medium"))
                            .to("stream:out?promptMessage=Medium priority message: ")
                        .otherwise()
                            .to("stream:out?promptMessage=Low priority message: ");
            }
        });
        main.run();
    }
}
Run the application and test with different messages:
// In a separate test class or main method
ProducerTemplate template = main.getCamelContext().createProducerTemplate();
template.sendBodyAndHeader("direct:start", "Urgent server issue", "priority", "high");
template.sendBodyAndHeader("direct:start", "Regular update", "priority", "medium");
template.sendBodyAndHeader("direct:start", "Informational message", "priority", "low");
Expected Output:

High priority message: Urgent server issue
Medium priority message: Regular update
Low priority message: Informational message
Troubleshooting Tip: If messages don't appear, verify the route is properly started and the headers are being set correctly.

Task 2: Splitter Pattern
Objective: Split a single message into multiple parts for individual processing

Create SplitterPatternDemo.java:
import org.apache.camel.builder.RouteBuilder;
import org.apache.camel.main.Main;

public class SplitterPatternDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Main main = new Main();
        main.configure().addRoutesBuilder(new RouteBuilder() {
            @Override
            public void configure() throws Exception {
                from("direct:start")
                    .split(body().tokenize(","))
                    .to("stream:out?promptMessage=Processing item: ");
            }
        });
        main.run();
    }
}
Test the splitter with a comma-separated string:
template.sendBody("direct:start", "apple,orange,banana,grape");
Expected Output:

Processing item: apple
Processing item: orange
Processing item: banana
Processing item: grape
Key Concept: The splitter breaks a single message containing multiple items into individual messages for separate processing.

Task 3: Aggregator Pattern
Objective: Combine multiple related messages into a single message

Create AggregatorPatternDemo.java:
import org.apache.camel.builder.RouteBuilder;
import org.apache.camel.main.Main;
import org.apache.camel.processor.aggregate.GroupedExchangeAggregationStrategy;

public class AggregatorPatternDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Main main = new Main();
        main.configure().addRoutesBuilder(new RouteBuilder() {
            @Override
            public void configure() throws Exception {
                from("direct:start")
                    .aggregate(header("orderId"), new GroupedExchangeAggregationStrategy())
                    .completionSize(3)
                    .to("stream:out?promptMessage=Completed order batch: ");
            }
        });
        main.run();
    }
}
Test the aggregator with multiple messages:
template.sendBodyAndHeader("direct:start", "Item1", "orderId", "order123");
template.sendBodyAndHeader("direct:start", "Item2", "orderId", "order123");
template.sendBodyAndHeader("direct:start", "Item3", "orderId", "order123");
Expected Output:

Completed order batch: [Exchange[Item1], Exchange[Item2], Exchange[Item3]]
Troubleshooting Tip: If aggregation doesn't complete, verify the completion condition (size, timeout, etc.) is being met.

Task 4: Combined Scenario
Objective: Implement a real-world scenario combining all three patterns

Create CombinedEIPDemo.java:
import org.apache.camel.builder.RouteBuilder;
import org.apache.camel.main.Main;
import org.apache.camel.processor.aggregate.GroupedExchangeAggregationStrategy;

public class CombinedEIPDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Main main = new Main();
        main.configure().addRoutesBuilder(new RouteBuilder() {
            @Override
            public void configure() throws Exception {
                // Split incoming CSV into rows
                from("direct:start")
                    .split(body().tokenize("\n"))
                    .to("direct:processRow");
                
                // Route rows based on content
                from("direct:processRow")
                    .choice()
                        .when(body().contains("ERROR"))
                            .to("direct:errorHandler")
                        .when(body().contains("WARN"))
                            .to("direct:warnHandler")
                        .otherwise()
                            .to("direct:infoHandler");
                
                // Aggregate errors
                from("direct:errorHandler")
                    .aggregate(constant(true), new GroupedExchangeAggregationStrategy())
                    .completionSize(5)
                    .to("stream:out?promptMessage=Error batch: ");
            }
        });
        main.run();
    }
}
Test with sample data:
String csvData = "INFO,Service started\n" +
                 "WARN,Low disk space\n" +
                 "ERROR,Database connection failed\n" +
                 "INFO,User logged in\n" +
                 "ERROR,File not found\n" +
                 "WARN,High memory usage\n" +
                 "ERROR,Timeout occurred\n" +
                 "ERROR,Authentication failed\n" +
                 "ERROR,Null pointer exception";

template.sendBody("direct:start", csvData);
Expected Outcome: The system will:

Split the CSV into individual lines
Route messages to appropriate handlers
Aggregate error messages in batches of 5
Conclusion
In this lab, you have successfully implemented three fundamental Enterprise Integration Patterns using Apache Camel:

Content-Based Router for conditional message routing
Splitter for dividing messages into parts
Aggregator for combining related messages
These patterns form the foundation for solving complex integration challenges in enterprise systems. The combined scenario demonstrated how these patterns can work together to create sophisticated message processing pipelines.

Key Takeaways:

EIPs provide standardized solutions to common integration problems
Apache Camel's DSL makes implementing EIPs straightforward
Patterns can be combined to address real-world scenarios
Proper message routing and processing improves system reliability
